<title>USA: Continental stake cut by FMR group.</title>
<headline>Continental stake cut by FMR group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by FMR Corp said Monday it cut its stake in Continental Airlines to 3,574,950 common shares or 7.48 percent from 10.74 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include the sale of 96,800 common shares between Nov 7 and Nov 20 at pricing ranging from $24 to $27.97 per share.</p>
<p>FMR Corp is the parent of the investment adviser to Fidelity Funds.</p>
